cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "miniVERL: verl for a single consumer GPU"
message: "If you use miniVERL in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.16.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/DaoyuanLi2816/mini-verl"
url: "https://github.com/DaoyuanLi2816/mini-verl"
abstract: >-
  miniVERL brings verl workflows to a single consumer NVIDIA GPU. It runs PPO,
  GRPO and on-policy distillation using documented verl configuration profiles,
  with native recipes for SFT, DPO and offline knowledge distillation. Training
  roles share the GPU in phases. Users can inspect rollouts and rewards, resume
  model and optimizer state exactly, and export PEFT adapters, Parquet data and
  configuration bundles. The repository includes reproducible systems measurements
  and task studies with their original data, methods and outcomes.
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Daoyuan
    email: lidaoyuan2816@gmail.com
keywords:
  - on-policy distillation
  - knowledge distillation
  - llm alignment
  - preference optimization
  - large language models
  - tool use
  - agents
  - PEFT
  - QLoRA
  - consumer GPU
  - single GPU
  - post-training
  - reproducibility
